CommonJS
A CommonJS module makes a function or value publicly available using
module.exports. For example:
// lib.js
const PI = 3.1415926;
// add values
function sum(...args) {
log('sum', args);
return args.reduce((num, tot) => tot + num);
}
// multiply values
function mult(...args) {
log('mult', args);
return args.reduce((num, tot) => tot * num);
}
// private logging function
function log(...msg) {
console.log(...msg);
}
module.exports = { PI, sum, mult };
Arequirestatement includes a module by referencing either:
its relative file path (./lib.js,../lib.js)
a fully qualified file path (/path/lib.js)
its npm name following installation (express,chalk, etc.)
The module is included at the point it’s referenced during execution of the
script.
